BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: three cases where a changed-date block
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:does not line up with a date its own series produced.
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:(1) The series is not in the file at all - some systems
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:send only the changed date. It is kept on its own, with
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:its own key, because it is a real event in the calendar.
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:(2) The series IS in the file, but the changed date names
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:a slot the rule never produced (here, a Wednesday in a
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:Tuesday series). It is added rather than thrown away.
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:(3) The series says that date was REMOVED (EXDATE) and a
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:changed-date block for it is left over. The removal wins:
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:deleting a date is a deliberate act by whoever keeps the
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:calendar, so the date stays out.
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:This file exists because the mutation run found that case
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:(1) stopped the whole import with an error, and no fixture
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:in the plan reached it.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:orphan-only-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/London:20261201T190000
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261201T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261201T203000
SUMMARY:Orphan changed date
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
